<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss sight deposits fall to 3,062.2 million Sfr.</title>
<headline>Swiss sight deposits fall to 3,062.2 million Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank said sight deposits fell by 1,865.2 million Swiss francs to 3,062.2 million in the reporting period ended January 10.</p>
<p>Statement of January 10 in millions of Swiss francs:</p>
<p>					 Latest   Change since Dec 31</p>
<p> Sight deposits		   3,062.2	minus  1,865.2</p>
<p> Currency reserves	     47,464.9	minus  1,075.0</p>
<p> Domestic securities	    3,095.2	minus	5.8</p>
<p> Notes in circulation	  30,225.8	minus  2,221.7</p>
<p> Other call deposits		460.7	minus    615.6</p>
<p> Government time deposits     2,225.3	plus   1,410.0</p>
<p>Borrowing at the emergency Lombard window fell by 759.2 million francs to 5.0 million in the reporting period.</p>
<p>Outstanding borrowing via the discount facility and swaps of money market certificates fell by 1,132.0 million francs to 449.7 million.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
